@title Observability Stack for 2027
@subtitle Comparison for the budget meeting, Copperleaf Insurance SRE
@author Site Reliability Engineering

We run 340 hosts, ingest about 2.1 TB of logs per month, and have 14 engineers on call. Three options are on the table: Datadog, Grafana Cloud, and self-hosted Prometheus, Loki and Grafana on our own Kubernetes.

## Comparison table

table = Option,Setup effort,Alerting,Log search,Lock-in,Annual cost; Datadog,low,excellent,excellent,high,"$412,000"; Grafana Cloud,low,good,good,medium,"$236,000"; Self-hosted,high,good,fair,low,"$148,000 plus 1.5 engineers"

## Three-year cost

data cum = Year,Datadog,Grafana Cloud,Self-hosted with staff time; 2027,412,236,418; 2028,865,496,706; 2029,1363,782,1004

chart line cum x=Year y=Datadog,Grafana Cloud,Self-hosted with staff time unit=K title="Cumulative cost, thousands of dollars"

Self-hosted includes the staff time for the 1.5 engineers. Once that is counted, Grafana Cloud is the cheapest of the three in every year.

## Pros and cons

### Datadog

**Pros**

- Excellent alerting and log search.
- Low setup effort.

**Cons**

- Highest annual cost.
- High lock-in.

### Grafana Cloud

**Pros**

- Low setup effort.
- Good alerting and log search.
- Dashboards stay portable.

**Cons**

- Medium lock-in.
- Log search is good, not excellent.

### Self-hosted

**Pros**

- Lowest license cost.
- Low lock-in.

**Cons**

- High setup effort.
- Needs 1.5 engineers to run it.
- Fair log search.

## Recommendation

Grafana Cloud, because it is the cheapest once staff time is counted and it keeps our dashboards portable.

! The Datadog quote expires on 2026-11-30. Self-hosted assumes we can hire the 1.5 engineers, which is not yet approved.
